-- Rifts World Book 33: Northern Gun One, five robots (printed 116-126): Bison, Blocker, Bruiser, Buffalo, Bulldog
-- 5 vehicle rows, with 51 locations and 19 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~286-northern-gun-1-robots-b.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-ax44-bison', 'Bison Combat Robot', 'rifts', 'robot', 'One pilot', NULL, 'Running 60 mph (96 km); leaps 8 ft (2.4 m) high and/or across', 'Not possible', 'Cannot swim; walks the sea or lake bed at 20 mph (32 km); maximum depth 800 ft (244 m)', 'Height 21 ft (6.4 m); width 10 ft (3 m); length 8 ft (2.4 m)', '12', 390, 1, NULL, 16000000, '21 million credits nuclear (new or nearly new, fully loaded), 18 million Solid Oxide Fuel Cell, 16 million electric battery; the lowest is stored.', 'Model Type: Bison Combat Robot. Class: AX-44 (Gladiator) Medium Combat Robot (headed AX-44 Bison Battler on p.116; the name here is the book''s Alphabetical List of NG Combat Robots, p.100). A crowd favorite of the Robodome gladiator pits, kept in its minotaur shape when NG turned it into a cheap commercial model five years ago. A close-quarters brawler: its broad, sharp-tipped fingers lock together into shovel blades that chop, stab and dig, and its Vibro-Blade horns and shock-absorbing neck make the head a battering ram. The pilot rides enclosed and cushioned in the hump, watching through eleven tiny hidden cameras (head 2, chest 4, hump 2, one per shoulder, back 2). Popular with miners, salvagers, raiders and mercenaries, and good against Xiticix inside their hives. The blade hands cannot use giant-sized guns; giant melee weapons are -2 to strike, parry and disarm. The forearm ion blaster can be swapped for an S.D.C. machine-gun firing silver-tipped rounds, and the shoulder plasma cannon for a laser cannon or a rail gun with a small payload. Robot P.S. 35. Cargo: a small locker for a rifle, pistol and survival kit, plus a water filter with a 3 gallon (11.4 liter) tank. Power: nuclear, 10 year average life; fuel cell and battery models too. Hand to hand per Light Ground Robot Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.353): restrained punch 1D4 M.D.; punch 2D4 M.D.; head butt 2D4 M.D., 2D6+6 M.D. with the Vibro-Horns on; claw rake 2D4+4 M.D.; karate chop 2D4+6 M.D.; stabbing or impaling chop 2D4+8 M.D.; karate power punch 4D4+16 M.D. (two attacks); stomp 1D4 M.D.; running ram 4D6 M.D. (+10 with the horns), two attacks, knocking down a foe of its size, smaller or up to 30% larger 86% of the time and one up to twice its size 60% (+10% if a leg was made to buckle); the fallen lose initiative and two attacks. Sensors: the standard NG robot features.', 'Rifts World Book 33: Northern Gun One p.116-118'),
  ('ng-v19-blocker', 'Blocker Combat Robot', 'rifts', 'robot', 'One pilot, with room for one passenger or gunner', NULL, 'Running 65 mph (104 km); leaps 8 ft (2.4 m) high and lengthwise, +50% with a running start', 'Not possible', 'Cannot swim; walks the bottom at 22 mph (35 km); maximum depth 1,000 ft (305 m)', 'Height 31 ft (9.5 m); width 16 ft (4.8 m); length 12 ft (3.6 m)', '28.5', 570, 1, NULL, 25000000, '32 million credits nuclear, 28 million Solid Oxide Fuel Cell, 25 million electric battery; the lowest is stored.', 'Model Type: NG-V19. Class: Infantry Assault Robot. A new design built as a walking linebacker, inspired by the shield walls of Sparta and Rome: it carries a huge slatted shield on its back, crouches behind it, and lowers it to shoot; the head is a laser turret that can fire over the top. Heavily armored with concealed chest missiles and pop-up forearm guns, redundant backup systems and a fire-suppression system that protects the pilot. Used to break enemy lines and defenses, as a sentry or rearguard, to stall robots and giant monsters, and for exploration and construction work; usually teamed with other infantry robots. The pilot sits in the chest, so losing the head turret does not hurt him. Robot P.S. 40. Cargo: a small locker holding a rifle, a pistol, a survival kit and some personal belongings. Power: nuclear, 20 year average life; fuel cell and battery models too. Hand to hand per Heavy Ground Robot Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352), plus shield attacks: shield strike 2D6+6 M.D.; power punch with the pointed bottom edge, two-handed, 4D6+12 M.D. (two attacks); body block with the shield 2D6+6 M.D.; running shield ram 4D6+8 M.D., two attacks, knocking down a foe of its size, smaller or up to 30% larger 90% of the time and one up to 150% larger 66%. Sensors: the standard NG robot features.', 'Rifts World Book 33: Northern Gun One p.118-120'),
  ('ng-v32-bruiser', 'Bruiser Combat Robot', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Two: a pilot and a gunner, seated back to back', NULL, 'Running 90 mph (144 km); leaps 10 ft (3 m) high and lengthwise, +50% with a running start, and 30 ft (9.1 m) above 60 mph (96 km)', 'Not possible', 'Cannot swim; walks the lake bed at up to 30 mph (48 km); maximum depth 1,000 ft (305 m)', 'Height 22 ft (6.7 m); width 16 ft (4.8 m); length 10 ft (3 m)', '22', 420, 1, NULL, 19000000, '27 million credits nuclear, 23 million Solid Oxide Fuel Cell, 19 million electric battery; the lowest is stored.', 'Model Type: NG-V32 Bruiser. Class: Infantry Assault Robot. Built on the Bison''s success as a heavily armored close-combat machine for city streets, thick forest, hive fighting and robot brawls, on sale for three years. Its signature is a pair of hydraulic piston arms ending in armored knuckles that hammer through walls, hatches, rock and vehicles while its gunner covers it with the shoulder ion turrets. The face holds two laser eyes, cameras and an infrared searchlight. A weakness few buyers know: destroying the head takes every sensor, leaving only the turret gun cameras, and losing those too leaves it blind. Robot P.S. 45 in the punching arms, 35 for lifting and pulling. Cargo: a small locker holding a rifle, a pistol, a survival kit and some personal belongings. Power: nuclear (the most common), 20 year average life; fuel cell and battery models too. Sensors beyond the NG standard: thermal imager, infrared and ultraviolet optics (all 1,200 ft/366 m), an infrared searchlight in the face (500 ft/152 m, aimed by turning the head), and four camera eyes with telescopic and macro lenses (4,000 ft/1,219 m) plus a gun camera on each ion turret, with image and video transmission.', 'Rifts World Book 33: Northern Gun One p.120-122'),
  ('ng-v34-buffalo', 'Buffalo Combat Robot', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Three: a pilot and two gunners, seated back to back', NULL, 'Running 55 mph (88 km); leaps 10 ft (3 m) high or across, +50% with a running start', 'Not possible', 'Cannot swim; walks the sea or lake bed at 25 mph (40 km); maximum depth 800 ft (244 m)', 'Height 25 ft (7.6 m); width 14 ft (4.3 m); length 10 ft (3 m)', '21', 510, 1, NULL, 22000000, '27 million credits nuclear (new or nearly new, fully loaded), 24 million Solid Oxide Fuel Cell, 22 million electric battery; the lowest is stored.', 'Model Type: NG-V34 (headed NG-V34 Buffalo). Class: Infantry Assault Robot. A mainline walking bunker for patrols, escort and guard duty, carrying enough firepower to beat armor without calling for help. Its horns are two particle beam cannons above the head, each with its own gunner; it adds forearm plasma ejectors, mini-missiles and fully articulated hands that use giant-sized weapons, tools and explosives. Every gun is short-ranged, so it shines in cities, tunnels, passes, ambushes and hives, and is torn apart in open ground by anything that outranges 1,600 ft (488 m). Sells well to mercenaries, town guards and small militaries. Losing the sensor head ends every optical and sensor system and all combat bonuses. Robot P.S. 35. Cargo: a small locker for a rifle, pistol and survival kit, plus a water filter with a 3 gallon (11.3 liter) tank. Power: nuclear, 15 year average life; fuel cell and battery models too. Hand to hand per Heavy Ground Robot Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352), with +2 to parry and +1 to disarm from the extra forearm plating. Sensors: the standard NG robot features.', 'Rifts World Book 33: Northern Gun One p.123-124'),
  ('ng-ex20-bulldog', 'Bulldog Combat Robot', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Three: pilot, copilot/gunner and a topside gunner', 'One more in comfort; 4-6 when cramped', 'Walking 50 mph (80 km) maximum; 70 mph (112 km) on its treads on smooth roads; leaping not possible', 'Not possible', 'Walks the lake floor at 20 mph (32 km); maximum depth 2,000 ft (610 m); the top turret works underwater only if its gunner has air and armor for the depth', 'Height 19 ft 7 in (6 m); width 16 ft (4.8 m) shoulder to shoulder; length 25 ft (7.6 m)', '24', 500, 1, NULL, 23000000, '31 million credits nuclear, 27 million Solid Oxide Fuel Cell, 23 million electric battery; the lowest is stored.', 'Model Type: NG-EX 20 (headed EX-20 Bulldog Explorer on p.124; the name here is the book''s Alphabetical List of NG Combat Robots, p.100). Class: All-Purpose Exploration Robot. A four-legged wilderness explorer, a hit since its release about eighteen months ago, meant for long trips by a small team. To travel on roads it rears back, locks its legs and drops a pair of treads. Sealed inside, it wades marsh and shallow water and can walk submerged, though owners seldom do. Aboard: four small private sleeping cabins, a tiny lab with a half-size refrigerator and lockable specimen bins, and a shared shower whose water is recycled up to 12 times; the pilot''s and nose gunner''s seats recline for sleeping. Up front, one big robot hand digs, clears debris, pushes and pulls, and two small arms with a light and camera each collect samples and do repairs; all three reach out a further 6 ft (1.8 m). The pilot''s cockpit is mostly M.D.C. plexiglass, with snap-on armor plates (small 25 M.D.C., large 40) that leave only a slit; one person fits them in about 10 minutes, two in four. A passenger can ride a jump-seat in the open top turret. Robot P.S. 40, small arms 28. Cargo: a 6x4x4 ft (1.8x1.2x1.2 m) bay and three 4x2x2 ft (1.2x0.6x0.6 m) exterior lockers; the cockpit and nose gunner can stow body armor, survival and first-aid kits, a backpack and 5 gallons (19 liters) of water, and more can be lashed outside. Power: nuclear, 20 year average life; fuel cell and battery models too. Hand to hand at half the attacks and half the Heavy Ground Robot Training bonuses (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352): giant hand 2D6+3 M.D. punch, tear or pry and 1D6 M.D. crush, no power punch; small arms 1D6 M.D. punch or tear, no power punch; stomp/trample 2D6+2 M.D.; a body block does 2D6 M.D. and has a 01-66% chance to knock down a foe of its size or smaller, who loses initiative and one attack. Sensors: the standard NG robot features.', 'Rifts World Book 33: Northern Gun One p.124-126');

